+{"schema_version": "1.0", "session_id": "39faadfc-108f-4032-afe9-c39356389017", "team_id": "contest2026_403_anpai", "github_login": "ma-abc123", "tool": "claude-code", "seq": 136, "ts": "2026-08-27T13:00:20.421Z", "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "tokens_in": 930, "tokens_out": 2697, "role": "tool", "tool_name": "Write", "tool_call_id": "call_6fbf7c36619142f188781e96", "input": {"file_path": "/home/ma/.claude/plans/eloquent-crafting-acorn.md", "content": "# AI Watch App Upgrade Plan\n\n## Context\n\nThe current AI Watch (`ai_watch_main.c`) is a single 1152-line file with a simple 2×2 grid app menu, home page clock, settings page, and basic touch/button navigation. It targets a 390×450 AMOLED display on the SF32LB52 board using LVGL v9.1.0 + NuttX.\n\nThe goal is to upgrade it into an extensible, app-based watch UI with:\n- A lightweight app registry (no framework dependency)\n- A honeycomb-style app menu (inspired by, but not copying, the SiFli example)\n- Unified page management with transitions\n- A functional timer app\n- Improved digital watchface\n- Touch gesture fixes so menu scrolling doesn't conflict with page swipes\n\nAll within a single `ai_watch_main.c` file (matching current project structure), using only LVGL v9 native APIs and NuttX POSIX APIs. No RT-Thread, no `gui_app_fwk`, no `cell_transform`, no SiFli GPU/EPIC, no custom_trans_anim.\n\n## Key Technical Facts (verified)\n\n- **LVGL version**: 9.1.0 (confirmed from `lvgl.h`)\n- **Display**: 390×450 CO5300 AMOLED (from vendor README and driver)\n- **API**: `lv_scr_load_anim` is a v8 compat macro → `lv_screen_load_anim` (from `lv_api_map_v8.h`)\n- **Fonts**: montserrat 16/20/24/28/48 enabled; FreeType enabled for Chinese support (`CONFIG_LV_USE_FREETYPE=y`, `CONFIG_LIB_FREETYPE=y`)\n- **Font path**: `CONFIG_UIKIT_FONT_LIB_PATH=\"/etc/data/\"`\n- **Build**: single `MAINSRC = ai_watch_main.c` in Makefile; Kconfig `CONFIG_EXAMPLES_AI_WATCH`\n- **Existing features to preserve**: BT toggle, theme switcher (dark/light/blue), about label with RTC status, KEY2 back/toggle, touch swipe navigation\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: App Registry + Page Manager Infrastructure\n\n**Changes to `ai_watch_main.c`**:\n\n1. **Add app registry struct and table** after the existing `ai_watch_s` struct:\n   ```c\n   typedef void (*app_create_cb_t)(FAR struct ai_watch_s *watch);\n   typedef void (*app_destroy_cb_t)(FAR struct ai_watch_s *watch);\n\n   struct ai_app_desc_s {\n       const char *name;\n       const char *icon_symbol;  /* LVGL symbol string */\n       app_create_cb_t create_cb;\n       app_destroy_cb_t destroy_cb;\n       bool available;\n   };\n   ```\n\n2. **Register existing apps** in a static table:\n   - Exercise (not available, shows \"Coming Soon\")\n   - Timer (available, with real create/destroy callbacks)\n   - Reminder (not available)\n   - Settings (available, navigates to settings page)\n\n3. **Add page management** to `ai_watch_s`:\n   ```c\n   /* Page stack for back navigation */\n   int page_stack[AI_WATCH_PAGE_MAX];\n   int page_stack_top;\n   lv_obj_t *current_page_obj;\n   lv_obj_t *app_page_obj;  /* dynamically created app pages */\n   ```\n\n4. **Replace `ai_watch_navigate_to`** with a unified page manager:\n   - `ai_watch_push_page(watch, page_id)` — push onto stack, animate in\n   - `ai_watch_pop_page(watch)` — pop stack, animate back\n   - `ai_watch_open_app(watch, app_index)` — create app page via registry callback\n   - `ai_watch_close_app(watch)` — destroy app page, return to menu\n\n### Phase 2: Honeycomb App Menu\n\nReplace the 2×2 grid with a honeycomb layout:\n\n1. **Delete `ai_watch_create_app_list_page`** and rewrite it.\n\n2. **New honeycomb layout** using absolute positioning on a scrollable container:\n   - Container: full screen, `LV_DIR_VER` scrollable\n   - Each icon: ~80×80 circle with symbol + name label\n   - Layout: center column at x=195, offset rows for hex effect\n     - Row 0 (center): 1 icon at (195, y0)\n     - Row 1: 2 icons at (195-50, y0+70), (195+50, y0+70)\n     - Row 2: 3 icons at (195-100, y0+140), (195, y0+140), (195+100, y0+140)\n     - Continue pattern as apps are added\n   - For current 4 apps: Row 0 (1), Row 1 (2), Row 2 (1 centered)\n   - Vertical centering: start y so first row is roughly centered\n\n3. **Scroll behavior**:\n   - Container handles its own scroll events\n   - No interference with global swipe detection\n   - Set `LV_DIR_HOR` to disabled on the container\n\n4. **Click handler**: use registry table to dispatch by index\n\n### Phase 3: Page Transitions\n\n1. **Replace `lv_scr_load_anim` with `lv_screen_load_anim`** (v9 native, though v8 compat works):\n   - Menu → app: `LV_SCR_LOAD_ANIM_MOVE_LEFT`, 200ms\n   - App → back: `LV_SCR_LOAD_ANIM_MOVE_RIGHT`, 200ms\n   - Home → menu: `LV_SCR_LOAD_ANIM_MOVE_UP`, 200ms\n   - Menu → home: `LV_SCR_LOAD_ANIM_MOVE_DOWN`, 200ms\n\n2. **App pages are created dynamically** as new screens (`lv_obj_create(NULL)`), loaded with animation, and deleted on close.\n\n### Phase 4: Timer App\n\n1. **Add timer state** to `ai_watch_s` or as a separate struct with static storage:\n   ```c\n   struct timer_state_s {\n       lv_obj_t *time_label;\n       lv_obj_t *start_btn;\n       lv_obj_t *reset_btn;\n       lv_timer_t *update_timer;\n       uint32_t start_tick;    /* lv_tick_get() when started */\n       uint32_t elapsed_ms;    /* accumulated when paused */\n       bool running;\n   };\n   ```\n\n2. **Timer UI**: screen with large time display \"MM:SS.CC\", three buttons (Start/Pause, Reset, Back)\n\n3. **Timer logic**:\n   - Start: record `lv_tick_get()`, set running=true, start lv_timer (50ms period)\n   - Pause: accumulate elapsed, set running=false, stop timer\n   - Reset: zero elapsed, reset display\n   - Update: compute `(lv_tick_get() - start_tick + elapsed_ms)` and format\n\n4. **Timer cleanup**: on page close (back), delete lv_timer, delete screen objects. State resets.\n\n### Phase 5: Digital Watchface\n\n1. **Redesign home page**:\n   - Large time: \"HH:MM\" in montserrat_48, centered vertically\n   - Seconds: smaller \"SS\" to the right or below\n   - Date: \"YYYY-MM-DD\" in montserrat_16 below time\n   - Day of week: optional, in montserrat_16\n   - BT status: top area, \"BT: ON/OFF\" with symbol\n   - Touch hint: bottom, \"Swipe up for apps\"\n\n2. **Keep existing time update logic** (`ai_watch_time_update`) but adjust label formatting.\n\n3. **RTC data reuse**: existing `clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME)` pattern stays unchanged.\n\n### Phase 6: Touch Event Boundary Fix\n\n1. **Modify `ai_watch_touch_update`**:\n   - On menu page: do NOT detect swipe-up/swipe-down for page navigation\n   - Let the LVGL scrollable container handle all touch events naturally\n   - Only detect swipe gestures on HOME page (up → menu) and on app pages (down → back, or use KEY2)\n\n2. **Strategy**: check `current_page` before processing gestures:\n   ```c\n   if (watch->current_page == AI_WATCH_PAGE_HOME) {\n       /* detect swipe-up → menu */\n   } else if (watch->current_page == AI_WATCH_PAGE_APP_LIST) {\n       /* no swipe navigation; let scroll handle it */\n       /* swipe-right or swipe-down could go back to home */\n   } else if (watch->current_page >= AI_WATCH_PAGE_APP_BASE) {\n       /* in-app: swipe-down or KEY2 → close app */\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **KEY2 behavior** remains consistent: always goes back one level in the page stack.\n\n### Phase 7: Resource Organization\n\n1. **Icons**: use LVGL built-in symbols (`LV_SYMBOL_PLAY`, `LV_SYMBOL_SETTINGS`, etc.) rendered as text labels — no image files needed.\n\n2. **Chinese font**: the defconfig has `CONFIG_LV_USE_FREETYPE=y` and `CONFIG_UIKIT_FONT_LIB_PATH=\"/etc/data/\"`. The existing code uses montserrat (Latin only). For Chinese display, we can use FreeType to load a system font if available, or stick with English labels to avoid garbled text. **Decision: keep all UI text in English** (matching current code style) to avoid Chinese font issues. The existing Chinese in the settings page's about label is already English.\n\n3. **No new resource files**: all icons are LVGL symbols, no new images or fonts.\n\n### Phase 8: Regression Testing\n\n1. **Verify preserved features**:\n   - Theme switching (dark/light/blue) works on all new pages\n   - BT toggle on home and settings stays in sync\n   - KEY2 navigation: home→toggle BT, menu→home, app→close app\n   - Touch swipe: home swipe-up→menu, menu swipe-right→home\n   - RTC time display updates correctly\n   - About label shows correct info\n\n2. **Compile check**: `build.sh` for the board config\n3. **git diff --check**: no whitespace errors\n\n## Files Modified\n\nOnly one file: `contest2026_403_anpai/app/ai_watch/ai_watch_main.c`\n\nNo changes to Makefile, Kconfig, CMakeLists.txt, defconfig, or board files.\n\n## Risks\n\n1. **Honeycomb layout precision**: manual pixel positioning for hex grid may need tuning on actual display\n2. **Page transition memory**: dynamic screen creation/deletion — must verify no leaks\n3. **Timer accuracy**: `lv_tick_get()` depends on LVGL tick period; adequate for UI display but not precision timing\n4. **FreeType Chinese**: not attempting Chinese labels; if Chinese UI is needed later, FreeType font loading would need configuration\n5. **Theme update scope**: existing theme update code walks child objects by index; new pages need to be included in theme refresh\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter implementation:\n1. Run `build.sh` to compile\n2. Run `git diff --check` for whitespace\n3. Review: all existing pages still accessible, new menu layout works, timer functions, transitions animate, touch/KEY2 navigation correct\n"}, "output": null}
