in v9, so I'll keep using that rather than switching to the native v9 API. I should also maintain the existing C style with the `FAR` macros for NuttX compatibility. The theme update function is going to be tricky since it needs to handle all the new pages, but I can walk through the children of each page to apply theme changes consistently.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering the structure—instead of creating new screens with `lv_obj_create(NULL)`, I should keep all pages as children of the main screen so the theme update can easily iterate through them. But that won't work with `lv_scr_load_anim`. So I'll need to apply the theme when switching pages, updating the current page's colors at that point.\n\nWriting the theme update function... I'm stepping back to simplify the approach—instead of dynamically creating and destroying pages, I'll pre-create all pages upfront and use `lv_screen_load_anim` to switch between them, reserving dynamic creation only for app-specific pages that need to be cleaned up separately. This way the theme can be applied consistently to all objects when it changes, and I'm restructuring the data model to track a fixed set of base pages alongside a pointer to the current dynamic app page.\n\nDefining the app descriptor structure... I'm realizing the existing event callback approach is getting unwieldy, so I should consolidate the app launch logic into a single callback that handles all the different cases cleanly."}
